+# Due Date Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Todos bekommen ein optionales Fälligkeitsdatum (`DateOnly?`): setzbar/änderbar/entfernbar über die API, anzeigbar in der Liste mit „überfällig"-Markierung, filterbar per `GET /todos?overdue=true` und per Checkbox in der Liste.
+
+**Architecture:** `Todo`/`NewTodo`/`TodoPatch` in `TodoStore.cs` werden um `DateOnly? DueDate` erweitert; `Todo` bekommt eine berechnete `IsOverdue`-Property (Datum vor heute UTC, nicht erledigt). Der PATCH-Endpoint parst den Body als `JsonDocument`, um „explizit null" (löschen) von „nicht gesetzt" zu unterscheiden, und validiert das Datum per `DateOnly.TryParseExact`. `Program.cs` bekommt den `overdue=true`-Query-Filter. `Home.razor` zeigt Datum + „überfällig" und eine Checkbox „nur überfällige".
+
+**Tech Stack:** .NET 10, Blazor Web App (interactive server), minimal API, System.Text.Json, xUnit + `WebApplicationFactory<Program>`. Keine neuen NuGet-Pakete.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-15-due-date-design.md` — this plan implements that spec; read both.
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- No new NuGet packages.
+- TDD: failing test first, then minimal implementation, then green.
+- Validation errors are `System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations.ValidationException`, thrown by `TodoStore` or the endpoint; `Program.cs` maps them to HTTP 400 `{"error": "..."}`.
+- Every UI element tests rely on carries a `data-testid`.
+- Error messages in English, matching existing convention (`"title is required"`).
+- `dueDate` is a pure calendar date `yyyy-MM-dd` (`DateOnly?`). Time components and impossible dates (e.g. `"2026-02-30"`) → 400 `{"error": "dueDate must be a valid calendar date (yyyy-MM-dd)"}`.
+- Overdue = `DueDate < DateOnly.FromDateTime(DateTime.UtcNow)` && `!Done`. Today is NOT overdue. No due date → never overdue.
+- `dueDate` is always serialized in Todo JSON, even when `null`.
+- Branch: `1_faelligkeitsdatum` (already created). Commit frequently, one commit per task.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+1. **PATCH `dueDate: null` vs omitted** — the `HasDueDate` flag must distinguish "clear the date" from "leave unchanged"; a mistake here silently deletes or never deletes dates.
+2. **Invalid date inputs** — `"2026-02-30"`, `"2026-10-20T17:00:00Z"`, `"20.10.2026"` must all be 400, not 500 or silently accepted; `DateOnly.TryParse` alone accepts some of these.
+3. **Overdue boundary** — a due date of *today* must not be overdue; done todos with past dates must not be overdue; todos without dates must never be overdue.
+4. **Existing exact-JSON test** — `TodoApiTests.CreatesAndListsTodos` asserts byte-exact JSON; adding `dueDate` changes it to include `"dueDate":null`. The test must be updated in the same task that changes the record, or the suite goes red.
+5. **UI filter must not mutate the store** — the „nur überfällige" checkbox filters only the rendered list; toggling it back must show all todos again.
+
+---
+
